  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Cgi Federal is an active federal contractor with $1.2B in obligations in FY2026 to date. Cgi Federal won 280 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $4.4M, and obligations are up 3.6% year over year. Department of State and General Services Administration are the largest buyers, with $240M and $239M in obligations respectively. Other major customers include Department of Justice with $149M, Department of Veterans Affairs with $136M, and Social Security Administration with $114M. Other Computer Related Services is Cgi Federal's largest market, accounting for $535M in obligations, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $269M and Computer Facilities Management Services at $202M. Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences are also material markets with $58.1M and $53.3M respectively. Fiscal-year obligations have been steady, with $1B in FY21 and $1.2B reported for FY24, FY25, and FY26 to date. The figures reported here are contract obligations unless noted otherwise.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Cgi Federal's federal business trended recently?",
        "body": "Cgi Federal's obligations were $1B in FY21 and rose to $1.1B in FY22 and FY23. Cgi Federal reported $1.2B in FY24, $1.2B in FY25, and $1.2B in FY26 to date, and obligations are up 3.6% year over year. Cgi Federal's award count for FY2026 to date is 280, with an average award size of $4.4M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Cgi Federal's biggest federal customers and markets?",
        "body": "Department of State and General Services Administration are the top buyers, with $240M and $239M in obligations respectively. Cgi Federal also has sizable obligations with Department of Justice ($149M), Department of Veterans Affairs ($136M), and Social Security Administration ($114M). Other Computer Related Services is the largest market at $535M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services ($269M) and Computer Facilities Management Services ($202M)."
      }
    ]
  },
